BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Workshop | Making Room: A Cyanotype Walk Through the Castro
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T130000
DTSTAMP:20261006T001200Z
UID:dothebay-17853532@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:LGBTQ
DESCRIPTION:LOCATION\n\nGLBT Historical Society Museum\n\n4127 18th Street
 \n\nSan Francisco\, CA 94114\n\nADMISSION\n\n$20 (includes materials fee)\
 ; Free for GLBT Historical Society Members*\n\nRSVP and reserve tickets he
 re\n\nInspired by Where We Made Room\, this workshop sends you out into th
 e Castro for a walking and blind contour drawing session\, capturing the b
 uildings and streets that have held queer life for generations. Back at th
 e museum\, we'll trace those sketches onto transparency paper to create ne
 gatives\, then head outside again to turn them into cyanotype prints using
  sun print paper—letting the sun fix your drawings into deep Prussian bl
 ue.\n\nJust as Landeta's silks layer archival exteriors with imagined inte
 riors to blur document and dream\, your prints will hold both what's actua
 lly there on the block and the loose\, intuitive line your hand found alon
 g the way.\n\nNo drawing experience necessary\, all materials provided. We
 ar shoes ready for a walk.\n\n*Due to the materials cost for this event\, 
 GLBT Historical Society Members are limited for one (1) free ticket to thi
 s program.\n\nPhoto: Jasmine Singh Rosado\n\nAleo Landeta (they/them) is i
 s a trans and Latine visual artist and educator based in Oakland whose pra
 ctice spans drawing\, painting\, installation\, and public programming. Th
 eir work centers queer joy as liberation\, drawing from lived experience a
 nd the communities that have held space for them to live authentically. Th
 ey have been exhibited at MACLA\, Bedford Gallery\, Berkeley Art Center\, 
 a...\n\n$20\n\nTickets: https://glbthistory.ticketing.veevartapp.com/ticke
 ts/view/list/film-screening-queer-spaces-we-made-a-shorts-glimpse\nDetails
 : https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/10/workshop-making-room-a-cyanotype-
 walk-through-the-castro-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
GEO:37.7608609;-122.4356584
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/34483965/fdca3ef5-1f00-4bd4-a85b-5e2f95fe9fc1.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T001200Z
LOCATION:GLBT History Museum\, 4127 18th St\, San Francisco\, CA\, 94114
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/10/workshop-making-room-a-cyanotyp
 e-walk-through-the-castro-tickets
END:VEVENT
